From: Armada / upstream 7.3, adapted for Asgard
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: LPASS releases its ADSP votes in sleep, so CX can collapse

Replaces 9040. Ported from Armada PR #723 (Odin 3, SM8750: CXSD + DDR LPM in
s2idle, 7.8 mA over 4 h):
- 0557-0562: upstream 7.3 (Ajay Kumar Nandam) wsa/va/tx/rx macros under the PM
  clock framework, so the q6prm LPASS_HW_MACRO/DCODEC votes the 7.2 drivers hold
  from probe drop in runtime suspend. On the Thor all four macros sat
  runtime-suspended with LPASS_HW_MACRO/DCODEC still at enable count 4.
- 0563/0564/0565 (sm8650 -> sm8550 LPI): macros, SoundWire and the LPASS LPI pin
  controller force-runtime-suspend across system sleep.
- 0531, rewritten for our sc8280xp.c (PRIMARY_MI2S_RX only): the board i2s_clk
  (the speaker MI2S) is dropped in suspend_post and retaken in resume_pre, so a
  PCM open at suspend doesn't keep it.
These votes are the ADSP's "AUDIO" DRV in the AOP CXPC violator list; with them
held, AOP never does CX shutdown (cxsd/aosd counts 0).

